  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="76.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 76.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ butan hit under þæs wifes cæglocan gebroht wære, si heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ buton hit under þes wifes cæglocum gebroht wære, syo heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et nisi sub custodia uxoris suę positum sit, ipsa innocens habeatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ buton hit under ðæs wifes cæglocan gebroht wære, sy heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And unless the goods had been put under the wife's lock and key, she shall be clear [of any charge of complicity].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And unless it has been brought under the wife’s lock and key, she is to be clear.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn es nicht unter des Eheweibes Verschluss (Schlösser? so A) gebracht worden ist, stehe sie rein da.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And unless it was brought under the wife's lock (locks?, so A), let her stand clean.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
